# Think in small steps

Java programs group behavior into classes and methods. Start with types, then expressions, then control flow.

```java
int count = 3;
boolean ready = true;
System.out.println(count + 2);
```

A method can take inputs and return a result. Practice one concept at a time. The offline runner supports a subset of Java libraries.

